ean\", ascending=False)\n","    )"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":9,"id":"a76354ca","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-08-17T06:33:02.011099Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-08-17T06:33:02.010631Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-08-17T06:33:23.721866Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-08-17T06:33:23.720682Z"},"papermill":{"duration":21.725774,"end_time":"2026-08-17T06:33:23.724055+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-08-17T06:33:01.998281+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"data":{"image/png":"\n","text/plain":["<Figure size 1500x400 with 3 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["fig, axes = plt.subplots(\n","    1,\n","    len(categorical_cols),\n","    figsize=(15, 4)\n",")\n","\n","for ax, col in zip(axes, categorical_cols):\n","    sns.barplot(\n","        data=train,\n","        x=col,\n","        y=\"addicted_label\",\n","        ax=ax\n","    )\n","\n","    ax.set_title(col)\n","    ax.set_ylabel(\"Target rate\")\n","    ax.tick_params(axis=\"x\", rotation=30)\n","\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"3b8625e0","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.010575,"end_time":"2026-08-17T06:33:23.745255+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-08-17T06:33:23.73468+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## Feature engineering\n","\n","After looking through the data, I started experimenting with a few features that seemed potentially useful.\n","\n","I didn't want to generate a huge number of arbitrary interactions. Most of the features below came from things that stood out during the initial analysis.\n","\n","### Missingness\n","\n","The dataset contains a fair amount of missing data, and I found it interesting enough to keep the missingness information rather than simply treating it as something to clean up.\n","\n","I added a `missing_count` feature as well as individual missing indicators for the main numerical/behavioral columns.\n","\n","The idea is fairly simple: **the fact that a value is missing can itself contain signal**.\n","\n","### Screen-time bins\n","\n","I also added a coarse version of `daily_screen_time_hours` by splitting it into several ranges.\n","\n","XGBoost can already learn nonlinear relationships from the raw value, so this isn't necessarily essential. I mainly wanted to give the model an explicit representation of broad screen-time groups.\n","\n","### `other_screen`\n","\n","This was one of the more interesting features I tried.\n","\n","The dataset gives us total daily screen time as well as time spent on social media, gaming, and work/study. I created:\n","\n","`daily_screen_time - social_media - gaming - work_study`\n","\n","I think of this as a **screen-time residual**. I'm not assuming that it represents a specific activity, but it does capture how much of the reported screen time isn't accounted for by those three categories.\n","\n","Two users can therefore have the same total screen time while having very different values for this feature. Adding this feature alone improves my XGB baseline.\n","\n","### Decimal precision\n","\n","The last group of features is a bit more speculative.\n","\n","Several of the numerical variables have values with different numbers of digits after the decimal point. Since this is a synthetic Playground Series dataset, and as suggested by numerous notebooks and discussions, the way these values were generated contains some signal that can be exploited.\n","\n","So I extracted the number of decimal places for several continuous features.\n","\n","This is a fairly cheap feature to add, so I kept it after seeing that it could contribute to the model.\n","\n","### Target encoding\n","\n","The other major addition was target encoding.\n","\n","I got the idea from [this notebook by tomasa2](https://www.kaggle.com/code/tomasa2/s6e8-what-moved-the-score-and-what-didn-t), where target encoding was tested as one of the approaches that moved the score.\n","\n","I tried it myself and it worked, so I kept it in the pipeline.\n","\n","I'm using smoothed target encoding with a smoothing value of `20`, which pulls estimates for low-frequency values towards the global target mean.\n","\n","The effect was fairly significant in my experiments. My initial LightGBM and XGBoost baselines were around **0.96507** and **0.96560** respectively. After adding the feature engineering and target encoding, the LightGBM result improved to around **0.96907**.\n","\n","This was enough of an improvement that I decided to keep these features in the final experiments rather than spending too much time trying to optimize the baseline models first.\n","\n","Here is the complete feature engineering function:\n","\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":10,"id":"2cc8d903","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-08-17T06:33:23.768387Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-08-17T06:33:23.768042Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-08-17T06:33:23.776891Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-08-17T06:33:23.775817Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.022778,"end_time":"2026-08-17T06:33:23.778938+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-08-17T06:33:23.75616+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["def feature_engineering(df):\n","    df = df.copy()\n","\n","    time_cols = [\n","        \"age\",\n","        \"daily_screen_time_hours\",\n","        \"social_media_hours\",\n","        \"gaming_hours\",\n","        \"work_study_hours\",\n","        \"sleep_hours\",\n","        \"notifications_per_day\",\n","        \"app_opens_per_day\",\n","        \"weekend_screen_time\"\n","    ]\n","\n","    # Missingness count\n","    df[\"missing_count\"] = df.isna().sum(axis=1)\n","\n","    # Individual missing indicators\n","    for col in time_cols:\n","        df[col + \"_is_missing\"] = (\n","            df[col].isna().astype(int)\n","        )\n","\n","    # Screen time bin\n","    df[\"screen_time_bin\"] = pd.cut(\n","        df[\"daily_screen_time_hours\"],\n","        bins=[\n","            -1,\n","            2,\n","            4,\n","            6,\n","            8,\n","            10,\n","            15,\n","            np.inf\n","        ],\n","        labels=False\n","    )\n","\n","    # Generator inconsistency\n","    df[\"other_screen\"] = (\n","        df[\"daily_screen_time_hours\"]\n","        -\n","        (\n","            df[\"social_media_hours\"]\n","            + df[\"gaming_hours\"]\n","            + df[\"work_study_hours\"]\n","        )\n","    )\n","\n","    # Decimal lattice features\n","    decimal_cols = [\n","        \"daily_screen_time_hours\",\n","        \"social_media_hours\",\n","        \"gaming_hours\",\n","        \"work_study_hours\",\n","        \"sleep_hours\",\n","        \"weekend_screen_time\"\n","    ]\n","\n","    for col in decimal_cols:\n","        df[col + \"_decimals\"] = (\n","            df[col]\n","            .astype(str)\n","            .str.split(\".\")\n","            .str[1]\n","            .fillna(\"\")\n","            .str.len()\n","        )\n","\n","    return df"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":11,"id":"cd54b2be","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-08-17T06:33:23.803311Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-08-17T06:33:23.80198Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-08-17T06:33:40.22883Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-08-17T06:33:40.227639Z"},"papermill":{"duration":16.441019,"end_time":"2026-08-17T06:33:40.230883+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-08-17T06:33:23.789864+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Train shape: (691369, 30)\n","Test shape : (296302, 30)\n"]}],"source":["X = train.drop(\n","    columns=[\"addicted_label\", \"id\"]\n",")\n","\n","X_test = test.drop(\n","    columns=[\"id\"]\n",")\n","\n","X = feature_engineering(X)\n","X_test = feature_engineering(X_test)\n","\n","print(\"Train shape:\", X.shape)\n","print(\"Test shape :\", X_test.shape)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"730a67c4","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.010458,"end_time":"2026-08-17T06:33:40.252093+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-08-17T06:33:40.241635+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## Target encoding\n","The other major addition was target encoding.\n","\n","I got the idea from this notebook by tomasa2, where target encoding was tested as one of the approaches that moved the score.\n","\n","I tried it myself and it worked, so I kept it in the pipeline.\n","\n","I'm using smoothed target encoding with a smoothing value of 20, which pulls estimates for low-frequency values towards the global target mean.\n","\n","The effect was fairly significant in my experiments. My initial LightGBM and XGBoost baselines were around 0.96507 and 0.96560 respectively. After adding the feature engineering and target encoding, the LightGBM result improved to around 0.96907.\n","\n","This was enough of an improvement that I decided to keep these features in the final experiments rather than spending too much time trying to optimize the baseline models first.\n","\n","Here is the complete feature engineering function:"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":12,"id":"1e947dcd","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-08-17T06:33:40.276601Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-08-17T06:33:40.275646Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-08-17T06:33:40.307079Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-08-17T06:33:40.306151Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.046384,"end_time":"2026-08-17T06:33:40.309024+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-08-17T06:33:40.26264+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["def target_encode(train_X, train_y, apply_X):\n","\n","    target_cols = [\n","        \"age\",\n","        \"daily_screen_time_hours\",\n","        \"social_media_hours\",\n","        \"gaming_hours\",\n","        \"work_study_hours\",\n","        \"sleep_hours\",\n","        \"notifications_per_day\",\n","        \"app_opens_per_day\",\n","        \"weekend_screen_time\",\n","        \"gender\",\n","        \"stress_level\",\n","        \"academic_work_impact\"\n","    ]\n","\n","    train_X = train_X.copy()\n","    apply_X = apply_X.copy()\n","\n","    global_mean = train_y.mean()\n","\n","    for col in target_cols:\n","\n","        stats = (\n","            pd.DataFrame({\n","                col: train_X[col],\n","                \"target\": train_y.values\n","            })\n","            .groupby(col)[\"target\"]\n","            .agg([\"mean\", \"count\"])\n","        )\n","\n","        smoothing = 20\n","\n","        encoding = (\n","            (stats[\"count\"] * stats[\"mean\"])\n","            +\n","            (smoothing * global_mean)\n","        ) / (\n","            stats[\"count\"] + smoothing\n","        )\n","\n","        train_X[col + \"_target_encoded\"] = (\n","            train_X[col]\n","            .map(encoding)\n","            .fillna(global_mean)\n","        )\n","\n","        apply_X[col + \"_target_encoded\"] = (\n","            apply_X[col]\n","            .map(encoding)\n","            .fillna(global_mean)\n","        )\n","\n","    return train_X, apply_X"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"50763ef6","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-08-17T06:00:55.636508Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-08-17T06:00:55.636182Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-08-17T06:00:55.64557Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-08-17T06:00:55.644649Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-08-17T06:00:55.636479Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.010393,"end_time":"2026-08-17T06:33:40.330292+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-08-17T06:33:40.319899+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## Cross validation\n","\n","With the features in place, I moved on to the main training loop.\n","\n","I'm using **5-fold StratifiedKFold**, and I repeat the entire process across five different random seeds.\n","\n","For each fold:\n","\n","1. Split the data into train and validation sets.\n","2. Fit the target encoding on the training split.\n","3. Apply the resulting encoding to validation and test.\n","4. Convert the categorical columns to pandas categorical features.\n","5. Train XGBoost with early stopping.\n","6. Store the validation predictions as OOF predictions.\n","7. Generate test predictions for that fold.\n","\n","At the end of each seed, I calculate the overall OOF AUC. Finally, I average the predictions from all five seeds.\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":13,"id":"ec41f3df","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-08-17T06:33:40.352833Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-08-17T06:33:40.352444Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-08-17T06:33:40.358351Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-08-17T06:33:40.357264Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.020056,"end_time":"2026-08-17T06:33:40.360664+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-08-17T06:33:40.340608+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["def makeModel(seed):\n","    model = xgb.XGBClassifier(\n","        objective=\"binary:logistic\",\n","        eval_metric=\"auc\",\n","\n","        n_estimators=8000,\n","        learning_rate=0.02,\n","\n","        max_depth=6,\n","        subsample=0.8,\n","        colsample_bytree=0.8,\n","\n","        reg_alpha=1,\n","        reg_lambda=10,\n","\n","        random_state=seed,\n","\n","        n_jobs=-1,\n","        tree_method=\"hist\",\n","        enable_categorical=True,\n","\n","        early_stopping_rounds=200\n","    )\n","\n","    return model"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":14,"id":"31ddd6d5","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-08-17T06:33:40.385747Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-08-17T06:33:40.384879Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-08-17T06:33:56.783568Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-08-17T06:33:56.782458Z"},"papermill":{"duration":16.412772,"end_time":"2026-08-17T06:33:56.785585+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-08-17T06:33:40.372813+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text"